<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria FEI Bank has 525 mln lev 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria FEI Bank has 525 mln lev 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's private First East International Bank (FEIB) posted a 525 million lev gross profit for 1996, the bank's balance sheet published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Under a shareholders' decision the total gross profit was set aside as provisions against the bank's risk assets.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for 1995 were not available.</p>
<p>Figures in million levs follow unless otherwise stated:</p>
<p>						  1996</p>
<p>Total revenue			    14,183.959</p>
<p>Net income on financial</p>
<p>transactions				1,374.761</p>
<p>Net extraordinary			   347.365</p>
<p>Business and administration costs   1,201.905</p>
<p>Taxes						 n.a</p>
<p>Profit					  525.007</p>
<p>Total assets			     31,015.640</p>
<p>Attracted funds from financial</p>
<p>and non-financial clients	    26,003.139</p>
<p>Financial assets, including</p>
<p>loans to financial and</p>
<p>non-financial clients		  23,822.559</p>
<p>Non-financial assets		    3,977.817</p>
<p>Shareholders equity		     3,000.000</p>
<p>Reserves				    1,105.428</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
